<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    What a thick rock roof leaves behind when it comes down (RimWorld: CollapsedRocks in
    Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Buildings/Buildings_Natural.xml, named by RoofRockThick's own
    collapseLeavingThingDef). RimWorld's description says what it is for: "Collapsed rocks, packed tightly
    enough to hold up a roof."

    That last clause is the mechanism, not flavour. An overhead-mountain collapse in RimWorld refills the cell
    with impassable rock, and RoofDef.VanishOnCollapse is false for a thick roof, so the roof stays and the new
    rock holds it — and its neighbours' — up again. The collapse is self-limiting: it cannot walk outward
    across a mountain, because every cell it drops becomes a support for the cells around it. This port
    removed the thick roof and spawned nothing, so every collapse permanently widened the unsupported area.

    Parents onto BaseNaturalRock, which already carries passability Impassable, fillPercent 1, category
    Building, destroyable=false and mineable=true — exactly what RimWorld's own RockBase gives it, and all
    that "holds a roof up, and can be dug out again by someone who decides to" needs. It stays mineable
    rather than being flagged off: mineable is also this codebase's line between natural rock and something
    somebody built (Map/ListerThings' BuildingArtificial group, and with it Settlement's own idea of where
    its centre is and WorkGiver_Repair's idea of what can be patched up), and collapsed rock is not a
    building.

    Like RimWorld's it names no mineableThing, so digging it back out costs work and pays nothing — the one
    Def in content for which that is the intent rather than an oversight, and Things/MiningTests names it as
    the exception for exactly that reason.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="BaseNaturalRock">
    <defName>CollapsedRocks</defName>
    <label>collapsed rocks</label>
    <description>Collapsed rocks, packed tightly enough to hold up a roof.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>500</MaxHitPoints>
    </statBases>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
